From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8280xp-blackrock: 512 MiB for CMA

A DRAM-less NVMe drive (Phison E13T, 1987:5013) took all of the
128 MiB CMA pool for its host memory buffer, and USB sound devices then
got no DMA memory. The Dev Kit has 32 GB: give CMA 512 MiB.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-microsoft-blackrock.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-microsoft-blackrock.dts
index 125af356e..679a97f63 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-microsoft-blackrock.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-microsoft-blackrock.dts
@@ -227,9 +227,13 @@ vreg_wwan: regulator-wwan {
 	};
 
 	reserved-memory {
+		/*
+		 * 512 MiB (was 128): a DRAM-less NVMe drive's host memory
+		 * buffer took all of 128 MiB, and USB sound got none.
+		 */
 		linux,cma {
 			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
-			size = <0x0 0x8000000>;
+			size = <0x0 0x20000000>;
 			reusable;
 			linux,cma-default;
 		};
